---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CategoryHub from '../../components/CategoryHub.astro';
---
<Base
  title="MEKP Hardener & Cobalt Accelerator Supplier in India"
  description="Samrat Poly Resins supplies MEKP catalyst and cobalt octoate accelerator for unsaturated polyester curing. They work together and must never be mixed directly."
>
  <CategoryHub
    category="Hardeners"
    slug="hardeners-accelerators"
    heading="Hardeners & Accelerators for Polyester Cure"
    eyebrow="Cure system"
    intro="Room-temperature polyester cure is a redox pair, not a single additive. A cobalt salt decomposes the peroxide catalyst at ambient temperature to generate radicals, and styrene then crosslinks the polyester into a rigid network. Samrat Poly Resins supplies both halves: MEKP as the catalyst and cobalt octoate as the accelerator."
    note="These two are not alternatives to each other. A resin that is already pre-accelerated needs only the peroxide; one that is not needs both, added separately and in the right order."
    gridHeading="Cure-system products"
    chooseHeading="Catalyst and accelerator do different jobs"
    collectionDescription="Samrat Poly Resins' published cure-system products for unsaturated polyester: MEKP catalyst and cobalt octoate accelerator."
    enquiryContext="hardeners-family"
    enquiryPlaceholder="Resin grade in use, whether it is pre-accelerated, process, working time required, quantity, delivery location"
    resourceSlugs={[
      'what-is-mekp-hardener',
      'what-is-cobalt-octoate',
      'understanding-gel-time-in-polyester-resin',
      'how-temperature-affects-polyester-cure',
      'troubleshooting-polyester-cure-speed',
      'common-frp-curing-problems',
    ]}
  >
    <Fragment slot="choose">
      <div class="hub-opt">
        <p class="hub-opt-name">Catalyst / initiator</p>
        <h3>MEKP Hardener</h3>
        <p>
          Methyl ethyl ketone peroxide. It is the radical source, used at a low percentage
          and not consumed stoichiometrically, so adding more does not give a harder cure —
          it gives a faster, hotter one, with the defects that follow.
        </p>
        <a href="/products/mekp-hardener/">View MEKP Hardener</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hub-opt">
        <p class="hub-opt-name">Accelerator / promoter</p>
        <h3>Cobalt Octoate</h3>
        <p>
          The cobalt salt that lets MEKP decompose at room temperature at all. Without it a
          cobalt-dependent system will not cure at ambient. Many resins arrive
          pre-accelerated, in which case this is already in the drum.
        </p>
        <a href="/products/cobalt-octoate/">View Cobalt Octoate</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hub-caution">
        The one rule that matters more than any other on this page: never bring MEKP and
        cobalt accelerator into direct contact. Mixed together undiluted they can react
        violently. The accelerator goes into the resin first and is stirred in, then the
        peroxide goes in separately. Peroxides also lose activity in storage and have real
        temperature limits, so check the age of stock before blaming a resin for a slow
        cure. Dosage belongs to the resin grade and the shop temperature, so confirm it
        against the grade's own data sheet rather than carrying a figure across.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </CategoryHub>
</Base>
